  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "While naïve art was often viewed (prior to the twentieth century) as outsider art produced by those without formal (or little) training or degrees, it is now a fully recognized art genre, represented in art galleries and academies worldwide. An equal accuracy brought to details, including those of the background which should be shaded off. Simplicity rather than subtlety are all supposed markers of naïve art. It has, however, become such a popular and recognizable style that many examples could be called pseudo-naïve."
  },
